        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-07T13:19:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this should return `maskBounds()`, or `bounds()` should be updated to actually return the masked bounds.  The bounds returned by `Geometry::bounds` are meant to be relative to the transform that\u0027s applied in order to draw it. For regular shapes, that\u0027s the full local-to-device matrix, but for special geometries that\u0027s not necessarily the case. \n\nFor instance, sub runs have a decomposed transform and are sometimes already transformed into device space. In that case, the recorded draws use just a translation matrix and the subrun\u0027s bounds are effectively projected to device space (sans the translation).\n\nThis is pretty similar to how AtlasShapes are drawn, where their \"shape\" is actually the non-zero (or non-one for inverse-fills) portion of the coverage mask.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 157,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 157,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "e640601c0645e82e8ffb672df798404366da6644",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
